{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he fled</b> — You might think that your father, when he fled to Aram, was poor. And thus he said: \"And he gave me bread to eat.\"" "<b>And he served, for a wife</b> — this is \"Did I not serve you for Rachel?\" And on account of a wife he was a keeper of sheep. And I made him wealthy; I also brought up his sons by the hand of a prophet — he is Moses. And Israel returned like sheep, and their keeper was Moses. And Israel forgot all this."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:05.630742698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}